meta {
  name: Upload Attachment
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/uploads/attachment
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(C:\path\to\receipt.pdf)
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.url) bru.setEnvVar("attachmentUrl", data.url);
}

docs {
  Upload one file to S3 and get its public URL. Form field name is **`file`**.

  The object is stored under the legacy **ezhealthtrack** key layout
  `{env}/{tenantId}/{YYYY}/{MM}/{DD}/{filename}` (UTC date; `env` = `prod`/`dev`/
  `test` from `NODE_ENV`), keeping the file's **original (sanitised) name** plus a
  short unique suffix before the extension (e.g. `lab-report_a1b2c3.pdf`) so
  same-name uploads never overwrite each other.

  Accepted types: PDF, JPG/JPEG/PNG/WEBP/GIF/SVG, DOC/DOCX, XLS/XLSX, CSV. Max
  **10 MB**, otherwise 422 `INVALID_UPLOAD_FILE`. Returns
  `{ "url": "<public-base>/<bucket>/<key>" }` (path-style) — stored on
  DigitalOcean Spaces, e.g.
  `https://sgp1.digitaloceanspaces.com/stage.ez.reports/...` (or a CDN/custom
  base if `SPACES_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` is set). Store that string wherever an
  attachment URL is kept (e.g. pass it as `attachmentUrl` to **Receive Invoice
  Payment** / **Settle Settlement**).

  500 `UPLOAD_NOT_CONFIGURED` if the server's SPACES_BUCKET / SPACES_ENDPOINT /
  SPACES_ACCESS_KEY / SPACES_SECRET_KEY are unset. Objects are stored public-read,
  so the bucket must allow public object reads for the returned URL to preview in
  a browser.

  Edit the `@file(...)` path to a real file on your machine before sending. Run
  **Business Auth → Login** first so `{{businessAccessToken}}` is set.
}
